<!--
    Wallet glyph with soft diagonal shading. Two-tone blue bifold wallet
    (lighter body, darker front pocket) with a centered thumb-notch scoop cut
    into the pocket's top edge - a real card-holder detail that replaces the
    generic round clasp button most wallet icons share, so the mark reads as
    ours. Two cards peek straight up from behind the top edge at staggered
    heights (yellow behind-left, red front-right). Each element is filled with a
    45-degree linear gradient from a lighter tint (top-left) to its base tone
    (bottom-right), lifting the flat look while keeping the brand hues.

    The whole artwork is wrapped in one group that scales it down and nudges it
    up, so it keeps a comfortable margin from the maskable edge and reads as
    centred in the frame. Draw order: cards (behind), wallet body, pocket band
    with the notch. The scoop shows the lighter body blue through the cut.
-->
